This program uses dynamic programming and caching to efficiently calculate the number of valid fuel tank combinations. It calculates two powers of two and determines how many of the `all_combinations` are not using the maximum volume. The `generate_valid_volume_combinations` function applies a logic similar to the Chinese remainder theorem for the weights in modular arithmetic. The `calculate_destroyed_subsets` function computes the number of subsets that prevent a valid patrol by iterating over all possible subsets.

